<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Sassari</h1><p class="st-meta">1272 CE – 1323 CE (approx.) · capital Sassari</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A self-governing Sardinian city-republic that rose from the ruins of the Judicate of Logudoro and wrote its laws partly in Sardinian.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelasia-of-torres">Adelasia</a> ended the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/judicate-of-logudoro">Judicate of Logudoro</a> in 1259, the growing town of Sassari took control of its own affairs and part of the surrounding territory. From 1272 it governed itself as a commune under Pisan influence, before allying with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-genoa">Republic of Genoa</a> in 1294.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The free commune was led by a podestà sent from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-genoa">Genoa</a> and local councils. Its statutes of 1316, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/statutes-of-sassari">Statuti Sassaresi</a>, survive in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> and Sardinian versions and regulated trade, farming and justice. Sassari lived from grain, livestock and trade through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-torres">Porto Torres</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1323 Sassari submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-iv-of-aragon">Infante Alfonso</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon</a> at the start of the Aragonese conquest, becoming part of the new <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a>. It revolted several times in the following years.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-sassari.jpg" alt="Republic of Sassari" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Ketipmaig · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Sassari_(1259%E2%80%931323).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1272 CE – 1323 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sassari</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sardinian, Latin, Ligurian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Free Commune of Sassari</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1298&amp;focus=republic-of-sassari" aria-label="Republic of Sassari on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4890 723 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Sassari lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5210 979L5206 976M5210 979L5214 863M5210 979L5226 1028"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5206 976h0M5214 863h0M5226 1028h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5210 979h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5210 979h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sassari. <a href="/atlas?year=1298&amp;focus=republic-of-sassari">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
